  "instructions": [
    "Cut the beef shin into 2-inch pieces and season with salt, black pepper, and paprika.",
    "Heat the air fryer to 400°F (200°C).",
    "In a large bowl, toss together the beef, onion, carrot, and sweet potato with the apple cider vinegar, brown sugar, and cayenne pepper until the vegetables are evenly coated.",
    "Transfer the mixture to the air fryer basket and cook for 20 minutes, shaking the basket halfway through.",
    "After 20 minutes, increase the air fryer temperature to 420°F (220°C) and cook for an additional 10 minutes, or until the beef is tender and the vegetables are caramelized.",
    "Serve the Slovakian beef shin hash hot on a hot stone plate, garnished with chopped fresh parsley if desired."
